+# Combined local rehearsal setup
+
+Use Python 3.12, uv, and Node satisfying web/package-lock.json (the jsdom
+dependency currently requires Node 22.22.2+, 24.15.0+, or 26+).
+
+```sh
+uv sync --extra fly
+uv run --extra fly python -m tools.prepare_flyvis
+uv run pytest -m "not slow"
+cd web
+npm ci
+npx tsc --noEmit -p .
+npm run build
+```
+
+In three terminals, start the mission and reflex from the repository root,
+then Vite from web:
+
+```sh
+uv run uvicorn server.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
+uv run --extra fly python -m reflex.server
+cd web && npm run dev
+```
+
+Open Vite's URL. Its proxies route /ws/mission and /api to port 8000,
+and /ws/reflex and /reflex to port 8001. Mission health is /api/health;
+reflex health is http://127.0.0.1:8001/health. Serving web/dist from the mission
+server alone does not proxy the reflex socket; use Vite for the combined demo.
+
+Follow the root README for Laya weights and optional Grok/Atlas credentials.
+Keep .env, models, logs, and caches out of commits. Without Laya weights the
+mission explicitly falls back to the rule policy. The fly weights must be
+prepared separately; no network requests occur in the running reflex.
+
+Keep CPU PyTorch in this project's .venv. For measured fly limitations and
+checkpoint provenance see docs/fly-connectome/STATUS.md and DEMO.md.
